    "title": "World Baseball Classic today: Every WBC game happening on March 15",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 4:54 p.m. ETFollow USA vs. Dominican Republic live: Keep up with score and latest WBC highlightsThe 2026 World Baseball Classic continues on Sunday, March 15 with the United States and Dominican Republic facing off in the semifinals for a spot in the championship game.The winner of Sunday's clash at loanDepot Park in Miami will face either Venezuela or Italy for a spot in Tuesday's final. The Americans beat Canada in the quarterfinals while the Dominicans crushed South Korea to set up this semifinal showdown.USA TODAY Sports is on the ground covering the 2026 World Baseball Classic, bringing you behind the scenes with Team USA and baseball's biggest global stars. Keep up with the latest scores and news all the way through the grand finale in Miami to decide the WBC championship. Sign up for our daily sports newsletter to get the biggest storylines straight to your inbox.Buy 2026 WBC ticketsWorld Baseball Classic games on March 15Stream the World Baseball Classic on Fubo8 p.m. - Semifinals: USA vs. Dominican Republic, Miami (LoanDepot Park) on FS12026 World Baseball Classic poolsPool A (San Juan): Puerto Rico , Panama , Cuba , Canada , ColombiaPool B (Houston): United States , Mexico , Italy , Great Britain , BrazilPool C (Tokyo): Japan , South Korea , Australia , Czechia , Chinese TaipeiPool D (Miami): Venezuela , Netherlands , Dominican Republic , Israel , NicaraguaOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Information in this article was imported automatically into a template written and reviewed by a USA TODAY Sports editor. You can send feedback using this form.",
